# Raphael, Most Attitude: "Whenever Raphael attacks, until end of turn, you may play a card exiled with Raphael." The
# permission changes no object's characteristics or controller, so it modifies the rules of the game and applies to cards
# exiled with Raphael after it began, for the rest of the turn (CR 611.2c). Turn 5: Raphael and an Ornithopter attack, and
# his attack trigger resolves with nothing exiled yet. In the declare blockers step Raphael, the Nightwatcher is cast for its
# sneak cost, returning the unblocked Ornithopter; it enters attacking, Raphael's alliance ability exiles the top card,
# Lightning Bolt, and Bot1 casts that Bolt from exile the same turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Raphael, Most Attitude
Ornithopter
Mox Ruby
Raphael, the Nightwatcher
Mountain
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Raphael, Most Attitude.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Raphael, Most Attitude > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile.Count = 0
[T5 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Hand.Raphael, the Nightwatcher.Cast(Ability: Sneak)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus
